  "scope": "Canonical A1 full-production q^-4 Gaussian on the fixed L=16 three-torus, six real coordinates for three complex components, fixed rho_regularizer=1e-12, embedded Pauli generators, exact spectral convolution, and the declared common symmetry-preserving multiplier class. Counterterm and bare-concentration follow-ups are reviewed separately at fixed production coefficients.",
  "theorem_boundary": {
    "field_regularities": "X belongs almost surely to C^(1/2-kappa) for every kappa>0; partial_i X belongs to C^(-1/2-kappa)",
    "one_form": "omega_A=dm_A-q_A d rho=(rho+eps_rho)dq_A, q_A=m_A/(rho+eps_rho)",
    "canonical_lift": "K_A is the geometric/Stratonovich reconstruction of omega_A(X) partial_i X from the canonical Gaussian second level X^a circle partial_i X^b",
    "convergence": "For every finite p and kappa>0, admissible common-even approximations converge in L^p(Omega; C^(-1/2-kappa)); dyadic subsequences converge almost surely",
    "zero_K_counterterm": "E[X^a_Lambda partial_i X^b_Lambda]=partial_i C_Lambda^{ab}(0)=0 for every common real-even regulator",
    "scheme_boundary": "The limit is independent within the declared common-even scalar class; component-split asymmetric approximations may carry an area/drift anomaly",
    "energy_boundary": "The lift defines K_A only. It does not define J_A*K_A, |K_A|^2, or the Class-II Gibbs energy."
